Package: katzenpost
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Katzenpost mix network
 Every katzenpost binary, each installed under a kp prefix so that no
 generic name is claimed in /usr/bin: kpserver, kpdirauth, kpcourier and
 kpreplica, the kpclientd client daemon, and the kpconfig, kpgenconfig,
 kpgenkeypair, kpgeometry, kpsphinx, kpping, kpfetch, kpecho-plugin and
 kphttp-proxy tools.
 .
 kpclientd gets a system and a user unit, and kpserver, kpauthority and
 kpreplica are template units, so one host can run several of each. Every
 unit ships disabled and unstarted.
 .
 An instance named foo reads /etc/katzenpost/<role>/foo.toml and keeps its
 state in /var/lib/katzenpost/<role>/foo, mode 0700, so two instances
 never share a directory. kpclientd.toml and thinclient.toml hold no
 secrets and are conffiles; editing them points the client daemon at
 another network.
